<article class="en-article"><nav class="crumb"><a href="/en/">English edition</a> / <a href="/en/library/">Popular library</a></nav><header><p class="eyebrow">ENGLISH RESEARCH · GAUCHO HISTORY & LITERATURE</p><h1>Is Martín Fierro Argentina’s National Poem? History and Meaning</h1><p class="lead">Martín Fierro is widely regarded as a defining work of Argentine literature. But calling it a national poem is not the same as proving a timeless official designation: the work's status grew through reading, criticism, education and public debate.</p></header><figure><img src="/media/fotografias-v3/la-ida.webp" alt="Modern editorial reconstruction illustrating the cultural world of Martín Fierro" fetchpriority="high"/><figcaption>Modern editorial illustration, not an authentic historical photograph.</figcaption></figure><div class="body"><nav class="toc"><strong>Contents</strong>{sections.map(s=><a href={`#${s.id}`}>{s.heading}</a>)}<a href="#sources">Sources</a></nav>{sections.map((s,i)=><><section id={s.id}><h2>{s.heading}</h2><p>{s.body}</p></section>{i===0&&<AdSlot id="article-02-post-introduction" kind="article"/>}{i===2&&<AdSlot id="article-03-middle" kind="article"/>}{i===4&&<AdSlot id="article-04-late" kind="article"/>}</>)}<section id="sources"><h2>Sources and further reading</h2><p>This article distinguishes documented historical claims, scholarly interpretation and literary representation. Historical material is linked to the source institution or publication; original Spanish verses have not been modified or republished in translation here.</p><ul>{sources.map(s=><li><a href={s.url} target={s.url.startsWith('https://')?'_blank':undefined} rel={s.url.startsWith('https://')?'noopener noreferrer':undefined}>{s.name}</a></li>)}</ul><p><a href="/en/martin-fierro-summary/">Plot summary</a> · <a href="/en/what-is-a-gaucho/">Gaucho history</a> · <a href="/en/library/">Popular library</a></p></section><AdSlot id="article-05-end" kind="article"/></div></article>
